###############################################################################
# QoL Compendium - .gitignore for a Project Zomboid Lua mod
###############################################################################

## Test harness build output
# The runner is compiled from tests/harness/TestRunner.java on demand.
tests/build/

## Generated assets
# Every overlay texture is produced by tools/generate_overlays.py from a fixed
# seed, so the generator is the source of truth. The textures themselves are
# tracked, since players install the mod folder directly, but the preview sheets
# the generator emits alongside them are not.
tools/overlay_preview.png
tools/overlay_detail.png

## IDE / editor cruft
.idea/
.vscode/
.vs/
*.iml
*.code-workspace
*.swp
*~

## OS cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

## Logs and crash artefacts, wherever they land
*.log
hs_err_pid*.log
logs/

###############################################################################
# Local-only reference material. NOT for publication.
#
# other-mods/ holds the unpacked source of every mod on the integration list.
# It is other people's work under other people's terms, and three of them
# explicitly forbid redistribution in any form, including as part of another
# mod. Publishing this folder would be exactly that. It stays local so the
# integration work can reference it.
#
# example-script-*.lua are the author's own scripts from an unrelated project,
# kept as a style reference only.
#
# Remove an entry only if you deliberately intend to publish it.
# See NOTICE and LICENSE.
###############################################################################
other-mods/
context-files/
external-files/
bug-reports/
example-script-*.lua
NOTES.md
